{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"The painting gallery is in the Louvre, — a straight, long hall, vaulted at the top — both sides hung with paintings; — a passage, almost endless, a quarter of an hour long; I had gone through it quickly with Cousin a few days ago, yesterday I wanted to begin the more thorough studies or views, when it turned out that exactly yesterday and today there is still time, — from tomorrow the museum (i.e. the collection of paintings and also the antiquities) is closed for preparation for the painting exhibition of current masters; — there is a great wealth and famous pieces by the noblest masters, which one has seen a hundred times in engravings, present; — by Raphael, Correggio, Leon. da Vinci, Titian and so on, — I am going back again in half an hour, to find Raumer!) and Panofka, whom I met there yesterday, and to make an appointment with them for this afternoon, it is Sunday and church fair in St. Cloud (i.e. fishing in Stralau)?) ; Cousin advises against going; instead there is horse racing at the Champ de Mars. — Raumer has an audience with Mlle Mars today at noon; he must be with all the actresses); Cousin finds it ridiculous to go to her, — to Talma or Mde Pasta, — if they were still here — he would have taken me. By the way Mlle Mars; in the theater I have of course also already been — in the French one twice, — once Alzire by Voltaire and l'école des maris by Moliere — so from the most famous pieces, — the other time in Emilia, tragedy after W. Scott, — an Emilia has Mlle Mars, — then Mlle Leverd (Queen Elizabeth) played, — especially the Mars very charming and noble, of course with peculiarity; one understands Mlle Mars and Leverd every word 7); they play, as the men in general also, much more restrained, with much less pathetic raging than our actors and actresses, — the men are mediocre, Lafond the most famous after Talma, almost like a butcher; — the French are generally calmer and more definite in expressing their feelings than we are, especially you; how often do I say to you, you should say and treat the matter without feeling, yet your liveliness often suits you quite nicely!"}}],"created":1795080699,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":499,"prompt_tokens":632,"total_tokens":1131,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-GTZl3XZRn8aLr9Wjk3CqHfSX6JI4FzqW","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":632,"prompt_ms":735.269,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.1634003164556963,"prompt_per_second":859.549362206213,"predicted_n":499,"predicted_ms":11911.63,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.918935742971886,"predicted_per_second":41.80788019775631}}